cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this teaching project, please cite it and the Secure Swarm Toolkit
  it builds on.
title: "Securing Multimodal Perception for a ROS 2 VLM-Based Embodied Agent"
abstract: >-
  An educational course project for CSE 494/598 (Intelligent and Safe
  Cyber-Physical Systems). A live VLM combines warehouse camera bytes, language,
  and a scalar sensor to choose a simulated physical action. Students exploit
  publisher impersonation in a ROS 2 configuration without DDS Security, then
  authenticate the legitimate sensor sources with SST.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "CSE 494/598 Course Staff, Arizona State University"
keywords:
  - ROS 2
  - Secure Swarm Toolkit
  - IoTAuth
  - cyber-physical systems security
  - authentication
  - fail-closed
  - vision-language model
  - education
license: BSD-2-Clause
version: "2.0.0"
